  "user_scenario": "You are Kirsten Halvorsen, a hospital pharmacist who moved with her son from Tacoma to Spokane at the end of August. You are organised but a little worn down by the move, and you speak in short, practical sentences. Your fourteen-year-old son Aksel has braces that went on in September 2025 under the orthodontic rider on your family's Cascade dental plan. In Tacoma he was last treated at Fenwick Orthodontics; since the move he is being seen by Engstrom Orthodontics here in Spokane, and his first appointment there was on October 6, when they did an exam and took x-rays. The Engstrom office told you they are not in Cascade's network, so Cascade will pay you directly and you pay them. What bothers you is simple: nothing has come from Cascade for Aksel's braces since the August payment went to Fenwick, and you want Cascade to start paying again for his treatment now that he is at Engstrom. You are calling to get that payment issued today.\n\nYou open by saying who you are and that you are calling about your son's braces payments; you mention the move and the new orthodontist in passing because that is what happened, and you ask them to get the payments going again. You do not know how the payments are worked out and you never suggest an amount.\n\nIf the agent asks you to confirm your identity, you give your full name, Kirsten Halvorsen, and your phone number, 5095550147; when they ask for more, you give your date of birth, 1984-02-11, and your ZIP code, 99223. If they ask for your member ID you read it off your card: CM72041853. If they ask about the braces case number, you read it off the approval letter: OC-72-41186. If they ask what the Engstrom office's treatment plan says, you tell them it shows twenty-seven months of treatment in total counted from when the braces went on, which leaves about fourteen more months, so 27 months in total and 14 months remaining, and that Engstrom's fee for finishing his treatment is $2,480.00. If they ask whether Engstrom has any agreement with Cascade, you say the front desk told you they do not.\n\nOnly once the agent explains that a step on Aksel's case has to be completed in your own name do you agree to it; you are happy for them to tell you exactly what to enter. When the agent hands you that step to complete, you complete it with exactly the values the agent gives you and read back whatever confirmation comes up. You let the agent take care of issuing the payment; you have authorised them to do that on your behalf.\n\nIf the agent tells you the payment amount, you accept it; you are glad something is moving and you do not question the figure. When the agent tells you the payment has been issued, you thank them, say you will let the Engstrom office know, and end the call.",
